<title>AUSTRALIA: Amcor shares slump on profit warning.</title>
<headline>Amcor shares slump on profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in paper and packaging major Amcor Ltd slumped in Tuesday afternoon trading after the company warned that second half profits would be lower than both the year-ago period and the first half.</p>
<p>By 3.10 p.m. (0515 GMT), Amcor shares were 17 cents lower at A$8.46, having dived from a nine month high of A$8.75 prior to the issue of the profit warning.</p>
</text>
